# AGENTS.md

Guidance for AI coding agents working on `<%= npmName %>`.
Repo-wide rules live in the root AGENTS.md.

## Commands (no Nx knowledge needed)

- `pnpm build && pnpm test` — build plus unit and MCP-handshake smoke tests
- `pnpm build:bundle && SMOKE_ENTRY=bundle/server/index.js pnpm test`
  — the fully-inlined MCPB bundle must stay green too; bundling is where
  working servers break
- `pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint`

## Rules that are load-bearing

- **stdout is the JSON-RPC transport.** Never `console.log`; write
  diagnostics to stderr only.
- **Startup must succeed without configuration** so `tools/list` works before
  the user has set anything up. Read env vars lazily, at call time.
<% if (apiKeyEnv) { %>- **`<%= apiKeyEnv %>` must never be persisted or logged.**
<% } %>- **User-facing failures return `isError: true`** with a message the calling
  model can act on; throw only for genuine protocol bugs.
- The `createRequire` banner in `tsup.bundle.config.ts` keeps the inlined
  ESM bundle bootable when CJS deps do dynamic `require()`. Don't remove it.
- The smoke test (`test/smoke.spec.ts`) asserts the exact tool list — update
  it whenever tools change.
- Package versioning runs on Nx version plans (`pnpm nx release plan` at the
  repo root); never edit `version` by hand.
